---
// The privacy policy for The Sheet (docs/sheet.md, docs/sheet-sources.md), the page Google's
// consent screen links to. Keep it in step with what the planner actually reads and stores.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";

const policy = "https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy · ${siteConfig.title}`}
  description="Privacy policy for The Sheet, Lisul Elvitigala's personal planner on lisul-elvi.com: what it reads from Google, where it's kept, and how to remove access."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="writeup">
    <header class="writeup-head">
      <a class="back" href="/">← Home</a>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
    </header>
    <p class="tldr">
      The Sheet is the personal planner at lisul-elvi.com/plan. Only I use it: it signs in one
      Google account, mine, and refuses everyone else. Nothing it reads is sold, shared or used
      for ads.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What it reads from Google</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Calendar:</strong> it creates and edits events on one calendar of its own
          ("Time blocks") and reads my other events so it can plan around them. Those events are
          read in my browser and not stored.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gmail, read-only:</strong> for the mail accounts I connect, it can list, search
          and read messages, and only when I ask Claude to plan my day. It can't send, change,
          label or delete mail.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it's kept</h2>
      <p>
        My tasks, plan and settings live in my own Supabase database, which only my account can
        read. The keys that let it read a connected mailbox are kept encrypted there and used only
        by its server. Mail itself isn't stored: it's fetched when Claude asks and passed to my
        own Claude app.
      </p>

      <h2>Google's rules</h2>
      <p>
        The Sheet's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs
        will adhere to the <a href={policy}>Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the
        Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Removing access</h2>
      <p>
        Remove a mail account in the planner's Settings, which deletes its key, or revoke The Sheet
        at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">myaccount.google.com/connections</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:elvitigalalis@gmail.com">elvitigalalis@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
